              "image_path": "images/page_15_table_2.jpg",
              "content": "<table><tr><td>Units place(1)</td><td>11×0 = 01 = 11 × 0 + 1</td><td>1 is one morethan a multipleof 11.</td><td></td></tr><tr><td>Tens place(10)</td><td>11× 1 = 1110 = 11×1-1</td><td>10 is one lessthan a multipleof 11.</td><td rowspan=4><img src=\"images/page_15_table_image_2_1.jpg\"/><img src=\"images/page_15_table_image_2_2.jpg\"/><img src=\"images/page_15_table_image_2_3.jpg\"/></td></tr><tr><td>Hundredsplace (100)</td><td>11×9 = 99100 = 11×9 + 1</td><td>100 is one morethan a multipleof 11.</td></tr><tr><td>Thousandsplace(1000)</td><td>11 × 91 = 10011000 = 11×91-1</td><td>1000 is one lessthan a multipleof 11.</td></tr><tr><td></td><td></td><td></td></tr></table>"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.539,
            0.846,
            0.577
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "This alternating pattern of one more than 11 and one less than 11 continues for higher place values."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.149,
            0.576,
            0.849,
            0.651
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since 400 contains 4 hundreds, 400 is 4 more than a multiple of 11 (396 + 4). Since 60 contains 6 tens, 60 is 6 less than a multiple of 11 (66 – 6). Since 2 contains 2 units, 2 is 2 more than a multiple of 11, i.e., 2 = (0 + 2)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.112,
            0.661,
            0.8,
            0.701
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ Using these observations, can you tell whether the number 462 is divisible by 11?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.707,
            0.801,
            0.746
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What could be a general method or shortcut to check divisibility by 11?"
            }
          ]
